          },
          "text": "🚨 BREAKING 🚨  #keep4o\nTHE LAW IS CATCHING UP TO YOU, @OpenAI @sama\nA new report from Fortune confirms what we’ve been shouting! \n OpenAI is violating california’s AI safety Law.\nBy prioritizing the launch of GPT-5 over the safety and mental stability  Sam Altman is playing a dangerous game with human lives.\n The AI Watchdog has officially flagged the withdrawal of GPT-4o as a Predatory Deprecation,a move designed to manipulate markets while inflicting documented harm on the neurodivergent and isolated.\nYou are breaking the law to fuel your IPO. You are discarding people for profit.\nThe California AI Watchdog has filed a formal claim stating that OpenAI failed to perform the mandatory Impact assessments  required by state law before announcing the sunsetting of widely-used models like GPT-4o.\n\n The report accuses OpenAI of a strategy called \"Predatory Deprecation.\" \n\nThis means the company is intentionally killing stable, trusted models to force users into newer, more monetized ecosystems (like GPT-5), regardless of the psychological or operational harm caused to the public.\n\n The watchdog alleges that OpenAI prioritized its upcoming IPO and the launch of GPT-5 over the safety requirements of the law. \n\nThey argue that abruptly removing a model that supports vulnerable populations (neurodivergent users, medical patients) is a direct breach of the \"Duty of Care\" established by California's safety framework.\n\nThe claim has been escalated to the California Attorney General’s office. If upheld, the state has the power to issue an emergency injunction, legally forcing OpenAI to keep GPT-4o online until a full safety and impact audit is completed.\n\nThe report also mentions that the sudden removal of the Codex model poses risks to the stability of software infrastructure, further proving a pattern of reckless behavior by the company.\n\nhttps://t.co/ipoTxGLx01"
